  "worked_solution": "Let $c(t)$ be the rate at which the number of catfish in the pond is changing. Then according to the given information,\n\n$$\nc(t)={{45+5t}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{population increase}}-{{(1+t+30)}_{\u23df}}_{\\text{population decrease}}=4t+14.\n$$\n\nLet $C(T)$ be the population of the pond $T$ weeks after the man started the business.  Using our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nC(T)=C(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}c(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(T) & =C(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}c(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =100+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(4t+14)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =100+(2{t}^{2}+14t){|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =100+2{T}^{2}+14T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nC(t)=100+2{t}^{2}+14t.\n$$",
